WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.604
The authors argue the right way to grade a graph
network is by the quantities it can compute.

00:00:05.684 --> 00:00:07.071
Equivariant polynomials,

00:00:07.151 --> 00:00:11.044
polynomials of the adjacency matrix that respect
node relabeling,

00:00:11.124 --> 00:00:17.034
are natural candidates: subgraph counts and many
structural features are exactly such polynomials.

00:00:17.114 --> 00:00:20.640
Knowing their full space, and which a network can
evaluate,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.980
gives both a fine-grained ruler and a to-do list of
missing operations.
